# Accepted Trivy findings for the Aaru image. Each entry needs a reason and an
# expiry date; Trivy reports the finding again once the date passes.

# filelock: arbitrary file overwrite via insecure database file reopening.
# Fixed only in filelock 4.2.1, but every unstructured release (0.24.0 through
# 0.27.34) requires filelock<4, so the fix cannot be installed while RAG
# document parsing ships. Exploiting it needs local write access to the lock
# directory; the container runs read-only with no other local users.
# Revisit when unstructured allows filelock 4, or drop unstructured.
CVE-2026-112940 exp:2027-01-31
